From 6d5131783ffc241d1a4abeff74d999965ffb0efc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:47:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fused_gr: STRATA_GR_DOWN_PF=2|3 keeps 2 or 3 tiles of
 weights in flight in the staged down projection (opt-in)

gr_down_staged_kernel loads the next tile's weights while it uses the current one, then copies them into the current
registers inside a `#pragma unroll 1` loop, so the loads of tile h + 2 wait for tile h + 1 to land: about eight
serial DRAM round trips a read on 41 blocks. gr_down_staged_pf_kernel<T, PF> unrolls the eight tiles and keeps a
lane's weights in a ring of PF + 1 register slots at compile-time indices, issuing tile h + PF at the top of tile h.
The activations' cp.async staging, the barriers, the per-lane sums (chunks lane + 32 q of tile h, ascending h then
q, the same dot8u and += per token) and the warp sum and epilogue are the staged kernel's, so the outputs are the
same bits; fused_gr_check compares the staged read with the plain one bit for bit before a card uses it.

Only the exact-token launches of 1..6 tokens (STRATA_NO_MULTI_GR unset) take it; 7 and 8 tokens keep the generic
kernel. ptxas on sm_86: PF=2 uses 80-114 registers, PF=3 121-138, no spills (the staged <4,true> kernel uses 80
with 8 bytes of spill). Unset (or any other value) launches exactly the kernels as before: the SASS of every
existing kernel in fused_gr.cu is unchanged. New ctests gr_parity_down_pf2 / _pf3 (staged multi read against the
single-token reads, now at 1..8 tokens); fused_gr_bench's hashes compare a run with the switch to one without.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
